# Branding

Sources: `packages/web/src/shared/lib/brand.ts`, `brand-defaults.lib.ts`, and `organization-branding.ts`.

- Use the existing branding owner for user-visible app names, logos, support links, and defaults instead of duplicating literals in components.
- Distinguish build-time defaults from organization-provided branding. Preserve validation and fallback behavior for missing or untrusted values.
- Theme colors use semantic tokens. Product identifiers, protocol names, and API paths are not automatically replaceable marketing strings.
- A new configuration value needs a concrete consumer and appropriate environment/type documentation; do not add branding options speculatively.
